From: shyalya <shyalya@turtle-server.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 08:11:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Split world buffs into independent per-buff timers

Previously all three world buffs (Zandalar/Warchief's Blessing/Dragonslayer) shared one timer, so they always became available at the exact same instant, and a frequent restart (e.g. the scheduled 8h restart) meant waiting a full new 2-3h roll each time - on a server that gets restarted often, the buffs effectively never came.

Adds WorldBuffTimerState (timer/warningMs/warned/firstSinceRestart) and a shared UpdateWorldBuffTimer() helper, called once per buff with its own eligibility check. The very first roll after a (re)start uses a short interval (FirstMinInterval..FirstMaxInterval, default 10min-2h); every roll after that uses the normal interval (MinInterval..MaxInterval, default changed from 2h-3h to 1h-3h). Each buff now rolls, warns, and casts independently.
